FSPEED-NOTE lane=gbdt-categorical arms=* metric=mismatch delta=2.000000 reason=categorical method: XGBoost partition search (enable_categorical, max_cat_to_onehot 1), LightGBM its own categorical split (categorical_feature) at its defaults (max_cat_to_onehot, cat_smooth, cat_l2): different algorithms from CTR
FSPEED-NOTE lane=gbdt-categorical arms=* metric=mismatch delta=3.000000 reason=input conversion inside the fit clock: CatBoost gets the declared columns as int64 (it refuses float categorical columns), XGBoost a pandas frame with one CategoricalDtype per column; ours and LightGBM take the float32 codes
FSPEED-NOTE lane=gbdt-categorical arms=* metric=mismatch delta=4.000000 reason=LightGBM min_child_samples 20 and min_child_weight 1e-3 stay at its defaults: at 0 (the gbdt lanes' value) LightGBM 4.7.0 aborts the first categorical tree
FSPEED-NOTE lane=gbdt-categorical arms=* metric=mismatch delta=5.000000 reason=codes are dense 0..k-1 within the train slice (our fit refuses a non-dense categorical column); a test value unseen in training shares one unknown bucket k per column
